* <bit> umbrella header:
*   Aggregates the granular per-symbol headers under
* /inc/djinterp/re_std/bit/. Mirrors the standard <bit> convenience header
* and adds no symbols of its own.
*
*   THE CONSTRAINT IS THE SUBTLE PART:
*   Every counting, rotating and power-of-two function here is restricted
* to the UNSIGNED INTEGER TYPES -- and that set deliberately excludes
* bool, char, char8_t, char16_t, char32_t and wchar_t, several of which
* are unsigned on common platforms. bit_internal.hpp spells the set out
* rather than deriving it from is_unsigned, because a trait-derived test
* would admit bool and char and would do so platform-dependently.
*
*   byteswap is the exception: it takes any integral type, signed and
* character types included.
*
